    </region>
    <region left="18" top="88" width="740" height="32" color="#000000" fontSize="12">
      <text lang="eng" width="740" fontFamily="Arial" fontSize="10">
        <content>
          <p style="font-size: 12px; font-weight: bold;">External Flow over a Cylinder</p>
        </content>
      </text>
    </region>
    <region left="18" top="142" width="740" height="32" color="#000000" fontSize="12">
      <text lang="eng" width="740" fontFamily="Arial" fontSize="10">
        <content>
          <p style="font-size: 12px; font-weight: bold;">Introduction</p>
        </content>
      </text>
    </region>
    <region left="18" top="186" width="740" height="84" color="#000000" fontSize="10">
      <text lang="eng" width="740" fontFamily="Arial" fontSize="10">
        <content>
          <p>Water was run past a cylinder in a recirculating water channel at six motor controller setpoints. The drag force was found from a tension gauge on the pivoting cylinder assembly, and hydrogen bubbles showed the flow pattern. The drag coefficient was calculated at each Reynolds number and compared with literature data. Uncertainties were propagated with the Kline-McClintock method.</p>
        </content>
      </text>
    </region>
    <region left="18" top="290" width="740" height="32" color="#000000" fontSize="12">
      <text lang="eng" width="740" fontFamily="Arial" fontSize="10">
